# Claude Code — personal/local overrides + agent worktrees (never committed)
.claude/settings.local.json
.claude/worktrees/

# personal-brand strategy layer — the owner's private positioning source. Its documented home is
# `tadeumendonca-io`, which has ignored it since that repo was stood up; THIS repo did not, and
# `CLAUDE.md`'s scratch taxonomy stated the consequence in its own words while nothing enforced it —
# "writing private material to `.brand/` here puts it in a tracked path in a public repo". Preventive:
# no `.brand/` has ever existed in this tree (`git ls-files | grep -i brand` -> no output at the
# commit that added this line), so this un-tracks nothing and repairs nothing.
#
# What it does NOT do, stated because the entry invites the wider reading: it does not stop `git add
# -f`, it does not reach a paste into a comment or a PR body (which is how private text has actually
# reached a public surface here), and it removes the one signal that used to exist — an untracked
# `.brand/` showed up in `git status` and now will not. The guard's errors all run toward refusing a
# commit; the lost signal runs the other way, and nobody sees it.
.brand/

# The ONE place for scratch files, and it does not survive a session — `session-scratch.sh` empties
# it at SessionStart. Ignored rather than absent so a scratch write lands somewhere named instead of
# somewhere random: the failure this replaces was an agent leaving `dist-old-qa/` at a repo path that
# nothing ignored, which dirtied `git status` and broke a local lint with 1480 errors from a bundle.
# A leak into a named ignored directory is a leak that costs nothing.

# editor / os
.DS_Store
*.log
